A release that gives a lender time but leaves the borrower it lends to where it waited,
since it looks for borrowers only of threads on a queue, which a lender never is.
The borrower waits on another queue than its lender's account says.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a place waits on another queue than its account says

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -636,7 +636,7 @@ static void release(uint32_t c)
             place_settle(p);
         }
         /* A lender waits on no queue, and its account may give the borrower it lends to time. */
-        struct place *h = p != NULL ? place_borrower(p) : NULL;
+        struct place *h = p != NULL && p->queue != QUEUE_NONE ? place_borrower(p) : NULL;
         if (h != NULL && (h->queue == QUEUE_SPARE || h->queue == QUEUE_SPENT)) {
             place_settle(h);
         }
